KZ3 patch 2097 (RSX pass 92): cursor hiding and mouse lock; native mouse look default on (the RE notes "Pass 92").
ENHANCEMENT. libs/input/pad_mouse.h: pad_cursor_decide (pure; host test tools/smoke/test_cursor_gate.sh): hide =
focused, not minimised, no title-bar drag/resize or menu loop, not closing, over the client area (any position in
borderless/fullscreen), KZ3_CURSOR_HIDE (default 1); clip = the same and mouse look on. libs/input/pad_mouse.c: the
window procedure hook answers WM_SETCURSOR with SetCursor(NULL) instead of patch 2069's ShowCursor count, ClipCursor
to the client rect re-applied on WM_SIZE/WM_MOVE/WM_DISPLAYCHANGE/clicks/mode changes, released on WM_ACTIVATE
inactive, WM_ACTIVATEAPP off, WM_KILLFOCUS, minimise, WM_ENTERSIZEMOVE/WM_ENTERMENULOOP and WM_CLOSE/WM_DESTROY;
cursor handling no longer needs mouse look; pad_mouse_attach posts itself to the window's thread when called off it.
KZ3_MOUSE_LOOK default on (=0 off). libs/video/rsx_null_backend.c: rsx_dm_apply reports each display mode
(pad_mouse_set_mode), the exclusive re-take on activation re-applies (pad_mouse_refresh).

